WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.480
It’s a bit early, but let’s use
Golden Week for a club overnighter.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.880
Then let’s go to the beach!
The beach!

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.550
But it’s still May.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.810
To think I’d hear that coming
from you, Murakami-san.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.760
Well, after all...

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.640
we’re over the deadline for the plot.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.850
Er, yes. I’m sorry. Really sorry.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.520
I am working on it,
but I’m rewriting...

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.290
If we keep falling behind,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.990
discontent will build up
between the members,

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.000
we’ll get disbanded for inactivity
by the Student Council,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.700
all our work and our club
will disappear...

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.510
Making doujin games?

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.000
Ah, it was harder than I thought.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.210
We sure were young back then.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.590
We had all that time
to use as we liked.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:50.930
Years from now, we’ll be
drunk and commiserating about it.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.720
Isn't your imagination oddly negative?

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.030
Honda-chan, will it be your first overnighter?

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:56.990
Yes!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.140
For now, you can relax
and let us handle it.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.900
Oh yeah, last year we went to Shii’s house.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.660
On Teru-senpai’s whim.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.070
Is that so?

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.030
We doing the same again?

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.320
I’ve got noisy kid brothers at my place.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.510
And you know how my folks are.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.320
If there’s nowhere else,
it’ll have to be my place.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.680
It’s small and messy though...

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.280
So we'll start with a major cleaning
and a room search this year too?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.800
We’ll be getting together
so that you finish the plot, okay?

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.340
J-Just kidding.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.640
You take things so seriously.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.140
U-Um...

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.720
It’s far and in the middle of nowhere,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.280
but you’re welcome at my house.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.850
So many paddy fields!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.100
I’ve never been
to the end of this line.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.400
Glad you made it, everyone!

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.110
Mrs. Sasai, good day.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:51.080
Oh, Tama-chan, good day.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.700
Thank you for the gift the other day.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.210
She's a good girl.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.520
You're welcome.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:04:00.340
Was it wise to let her join this harsh world of game creation?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.920
Say, Murakami-san, didn’t you
overpack a bit?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.720
I figured I could take the chance
to set up some gear at Honda-san’s house,

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:16.180
add a server back-up and stuff to that in case you can’t get a signal here...

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.350
Cell phones can connect here.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:21.980
And on the off chance a bear comes,

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.560
I have several repellents...

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.740
W-we ain’t that rural!

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.000
You ain’t?

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.000
Sorry, just forget it.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.370
Plus a few provisions.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.020
I must say, you came prepared.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.260
This is my house.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.390
It’s huge!

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:52.840
You’re Tamaki’s friends?
Make yourselves at home, okay?

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.430
This is my grandma.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.720
Hello, thank you for having us.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.180
This is just a token
of our appreciation.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.860
You’re so young, but
you have such good manners!

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.200
She seems like a kind grandma.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.200
She's really nice. I love her.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.410
Are you alone here?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:17.910
Her father is posted elsewhere and
her mother is at work today.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.290
I see.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.540
So, what’re you doing here?

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:26.310
Wherever Tama-chan goes, Yumine will be found.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:26.960
Huh?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.130
This could be good
material for backgrounds.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.890
Hey, don’t be too bad mannered.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.600
Thank you for coming so far.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.600
Is that matcha? You made it?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.610
Yes! Mom got the snacks.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:50.070
She won't be here until later because of work, but she says hello.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.820
Whoa, it’s sweet!
This tastes like matcha ice cream!

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.500
Isn’t that the wrong way round?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.960
It tastes so good.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.870
If I mixed it with the drink I brought,
what flavor would I get?

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.260
Don’t you dare!
That’s beyond bad manners.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.590
This PC is much older
than I expected.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.380
It’s Dad’s old one.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:17.410
He said I could use it however I liked.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.180
I’ve basically finished setting up for now.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.140
Shared folders, a chat app,
and some hardware.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:28.480
Thank you. I seem to have gotten
rather a lot from you.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.480
It’s okay. I wasn’t using any of them.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.530
Oh, a pen tablet.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:38.450
In other words, now draw lots
of nice images with this?

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:45.420
So...

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.290
This is the next game
we’re going to create...

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.750
It’s an adventure game.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.280
It’ll be like a short side story
to last year’s game.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:56.720
Adventure?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.240
I get it!

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.310
Ah, not quite.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.060
You don't have to comment, Shii.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:09.980
By adventure, we mean the genre
also called ADV or a visual novel.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.940
It's like a picture show
with sound and images.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.950
The story branches depending
on actions such as choices...

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.990
Shii, your explanation
is too vague.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.870
Recent games have more gimmicks.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.620
I’m not into VNs, so I can’t help it.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.300
Choices?

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.550
I get it!

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.020
You really like the minecart element!

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.910
We’re at the stage of deciding the game’s design.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.480
Such as coming up with ideas for
what kind of game it’ll be.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.570
It’s like we really are working as a team.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:56.240
Right? It genuinely feels like
you’re creating a game now, right?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.320
Yes! This is exciting!

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.740
I knew it!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.310
We’re supposed to start with scheduling.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:07.540
Work schedule? Estimates?
I just write until I finish. Easy!

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.050
Actually, compared to last year,
she’s made progress.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.960
Let me remind you. The purpose
for this overnighter is...

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.720
Come up with a plot! I know.
I’ll get right to it!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.480
Having said that...

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.890
I can't think of anything!
But I’m so close!

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:32.350
I’m behind schedule because
I dropped the love-comedy plot.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:36.450
But with this new idea,
the ending’s not coming together.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.990
Even if I take just the ending
from the last one...

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:40.910
Say...

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.790
Do you really have to agonize
so much over the plot?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.250
It’s a short story, right?

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:52.170
I think that last idea was fine.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.340
After looking over it...

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:58.720
I thought we ought to go with something
that suits Honda-san’s drawings more.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:05.580
Anyway, I want to know soon
what’s needed for the music.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:09.460
Since I’m free, I might create a bunch
of weird music and play that at the climax.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.240
Sorry.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.440
Huh? A mic?

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:18.800
And... I might switch the snare sample to this.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:28.420
O-okay, I’ll have something by today.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.120
How dare you play with the bamboo clacker?!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.300
Who is it?

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:45.180
And... if you set the blend mode to “multiply,”

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.900
Oh, you’re right.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.660
It’s getting close to dinnertime,
so I’m going home.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.620
Just do as I showed you.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.500
Okay. Thank you, Yumine!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.860
See you.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:07.760
Um, next... put the highlight...

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.130
I can’t concentrate.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:21.650
B-by the way...
Why is it named the SNS Club?

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:24.120
Oh, last year’s president...

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.700
The club application was due yesterday?!

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:31.790
Yes. I’ll go to the Student Council
and apologize.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:34.460
But we don’t have a club name yet.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:38.170
You first years can decide.
Just fill it in with something random.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.720
Well. This is the only way.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.170
And regardless of the name, no hard feelings later.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.760
Ready, set...!

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.270
And so three slips written
by me were drawn.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.800
Why are they all negative terms?

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:08.450
It’s hard to draw lines
on a pen tablet.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:16.270
A pen tablet is essential when drawing
on a PC, but it’s tough with that alone.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.910
I guess it’s hard to draw pretty pictures.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.310
I’m sorry! I was fooling around...

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:38.200
From the beginning,

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:44.690
this club was formed on the whim of
the previous president, Teru-senpai.

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:49.310
This is my friend.
She’s a programmer.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:52.670
At first, I considered it a nuisance.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:56.140
But last year was so fulfilling.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:12:00.210
Now, I think it’d be a bit boring
without the club.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:05.880
This picture is part of my diary.
I’ll keep it as long as I’m alive.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:10.470
Um, t-that would be a bit embarrassing.

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.090
I just...

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:19.600
I just want to make this a club where
none of you will get bored.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.630
So please don’t get too
hung up on quality.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.930
Saying it’s “just” a club activity
may not sound good,

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.630
but going forward...

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:32.310
Please prioritize finishing the game.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.500
But I’m not sure whether
I can draw decent art...

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:41.380
Actually, I agree.
You may need a scanner.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:42.380
Scanner?

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.720
It scans pictures that you draw.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:48.420
But the characters’ faces
can be actual photos.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.870
That photo I took is good.
I could cut your face out from it...

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.670
Please stop!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.520
The president tends to be
on the pessimistic side...

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:06.140
but she’s a romanticist and playful,
yet very diligent.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.650
You’re a funny’un, President.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.660
R-really?

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.100
Oops, did I slip into my dialect just now?

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.560
A little.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.770
I’m so embarrassed.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.790
You can’t judge people by their looks.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.460
Oh man...

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.300
Seriously, you can’t judge people
by their looks.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:29.880
What happened?

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.170
Did you see a bear or something?

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:43.560
I made this chirashi sushi.
Please eat up.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.650
It’s huge!

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.840
It has a lot of impact!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.650
Mom’s chirashi sushi is really good.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:54.870
My daughter’s never been in a club before, and she has a lot to learn.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.990
Please support her.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:59.360
Same here. It’s our pleasure.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:04.350
Okay, relax and enjoy.
I need to go heat the bath.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:06.240
Your mom seems really nice too.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.950
Yes! Mom, Dad, and Grandma are all very kind.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.290
Who are you?!

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.890
Oh, it’s you, Seki-senpai.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.760
Hey, Honda-san, thanks for letting us use of your bathroom.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:27.220
Um, so, er...

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.920
I’m back!

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.320
Here’s the finished plot.
I printed it at the convenience store.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:34.310
Well, I’m off to the bath.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.530
We’re passing the plot around now.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:41.620
You could have printed enough for all of us.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.290
Just one’s a hassle.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:44.640
Hey, it’s not free.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.780
And I wondered if this plot was
worth being put onto paper.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:50.220
A bit late for that, isn't it?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:53.220
Okay, Honda-chan, shall we read it?

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.590
Umm... In a certain place...

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.790
Stop! Read it silently!

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:07.020
In a certain place, in the world of
a certain romance game...

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:11.890
Lived protagonist Samyu and heroine Stella, who just became his girlfriend.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.370
However, the player of this game

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.710
stopped playing there and a year has passed.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.540
It’s rather meta.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:34.420
I'm sick of waiting for a scenario that won't continue in this game that no one is playing!

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.700
Stella, let’s escape together!

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.930
But sadly, Stella, the heroine,
suffered from a chronic disease.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:42.890
I forgot to tell you, but...

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.430
if something near me
emits strong emotions,

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:48.210
an incurable disease
makes me say them out loud.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:50.800
What?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:54.180
So you feel emotions from
things other than people?

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:58.520
Yes. I think it’s my role
in this game world.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:01.640
Like the feelings of
that guy over there?

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.210
S-she’s watching me.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:12.110
Why is she staring at me?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:16.000
My delicate extremity...
My thick and unsightly shaft...

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.040
Every inch of me...

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.720
This wonderful feeling!
Go even deeper!

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.600
I don’t need to be dressed
in leaves or flowers!

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.890
That’s the tree, not the cat talking!

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:28.050
The gags are impure!

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.440
Samyu and Stella go about doing
research to find a treatment.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.280
But they can’t seem to find any cure.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.620
Stella steps out of
her destined scenario for the first time...

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.700
and is deluged with the feelings
of a myriad of things in the world outside...

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.870
and begins to turn pale.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:54.850
Samyu works desperately for her sake.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.060
And she supports him,
even as she weakens.

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.720
And before they know it...

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.170
Samyu-kun, thank you for all you do.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:14.850
If it’s okay with you,
I’d like to stay with you forever.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:20.140
I wonder if this feeling is
what’s called affection level.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.430
Samyu faces a decision.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.850
Their future.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:28.810
However...

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:33.540
<i>Damn it! By being indecisive,
I made a selection appear!</i>

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:39.210
<i>I’ve given the decision to the player,
but there isn’t one anymore!</i>

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:44.370
<i>No one can make this selection,
so I’m stuck here!</i>

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.380
Samyu’s adventure comes to an end here.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:54.350
What kind of outcome is this?!
It’s so meta!

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:56.940
That’s a bad end! There’s more!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.700
Er... Once a certain condition is met,
the story moves on.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.550
You seem at a loss, sir.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.660
<i>The selection window just spoke!</i>

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:11.500
The way you defied the scenario
and made your own path...

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.930
was most splendid.

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:18.330
I have witnessed the twists and turns
of myriad stories.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.420
I must push you forward...

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:24.710
Or I’m not a man!

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:30.470
No more hesitation.
Stella, let’s stay together forever.

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:32.930
I’m so happy.
I’ve waited for those words!

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:37.420
I...

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:42.230
<i>Way to go, bro! Now get in bed...</i>

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:44.720
Oh, that’s...

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.240
I’m sorry, I did it again...

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.420
It’s okay.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:54.040
It’ll be a hard road,
but let’s walk it together.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.620
Let’s continue to defy fate.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:04.740
T-that's a happy ending... right?

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:08.480
The theme is that there's always
more than meets the eye.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.500
Who’s that?!

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:11.430
Oh, like earlier...

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:14.460
Oh and, we talked about
adding an old man.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:15.600
So here.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.650
Congratulations.
I will always watch over you.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:27.180
Isn’t that pointless?
It’s blatantly tacked on!

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.280
I think it’s great!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.650
Seriously? You approve?!

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:37.870
So how do we split up
the bad end and true end?

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:40.040
Was there somewhere
it could branch?

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.660
See, that’s it.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:45.760
The story’s about what lies outside of fate.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:50.910
So I figured a system where it branches
from choices inside the game would be weird.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.810
And so, when you play this game...

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:57.480
A “true.exe” appears on the PC desktop.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.520
When you double-click that
you can get the true end.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:01.190
It sucks.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:02.690
What is it? Sounds like a virus.

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:04.290
I guess...

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.450
Anyway, good job.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.950
It’ll be great if we can add
interesting elements to this.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:10.990
Yeah.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:14.310
I think it’d be good to expand on
hearing the voices of things.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:15.800
We can have various things talk.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:19.460
I have a feeling it'll get more impure.

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:21.320
That’s what makes it interesting.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:25.170
If there were more times when things
that talk showed up as people,

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.420
I think that would make it more fun.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.090
Good! Great! Nice!

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:32.470
Yeah! Congratulations!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:35.830
We could, but they don’t have
to be old men, right?

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:40.230
And put in shipping fuel between
hot guys to appeal to fujoshi.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.660
When did you come back?

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:45.340
Oh yeah, Seki-san, what was that one you
read out loud in the club room?

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:50.850
Ah, this is our first game together...
and that one’s too big in scale...

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.450
We should start smaller...

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:57.570
Admirable prudence.
I’d rather you realized sooner though.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:20:59.950
Is this the one?

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.580
“Behold, the evening dew on this Leontochir flower...”

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:05.500
STOP!!!

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.660
That’s not it!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.290
How about some tea and snacks?

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.800
Are you okay?!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.500
What?!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:20.390
You again?!

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.550
Sorry, sorry!

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.180
Things got messy with tea and all,

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.350
so we went to a bath house.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:37.940
I’m really sorry about our behavior.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:40.250
We’ve spoiled our stay.

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.440
It wasn’t your fault.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:47.550
But Seki-senpai got her story idea on this overnighter, so I'm happy.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:49.130
I have to do my best too.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.680
First, I’ll draw Selection Window-san.

00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:57.590
Those two are getting along nicely.

00:21:58.820 --> 00:22:01.400
Fujikawa-san? I wasn’t sure who it was.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:06.540
Well now, that’s an interesting element.

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.040
The senpai and her kouhai...

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:15.070
Yuri. Not a bad idea.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:17.560
Hold on, just what are you shipping?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:22.200
I misjudged you, Senpai!
Is that how you see Tama-chan?!

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:23.420
Come on...

00:22:23.420 --> 00:22:26.030
I just thought a story like that
might be good.

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:27.980
Tama-chan...

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.630
...is the seme!

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.240
If you make her male,
he’d be kind of slim and delicate...

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.590
but in bed he’s always on top!

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:37.740
Ah, but as a sasoi-uke is also...

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:41.620
You’re the one looking at her indecently!

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:41.620
Is there a reason for changing gender?

00:23:02.350 --> 00:23:05.110
Today was fun, Senpai.

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:11.740
I’ll practice what I was taught
for a little while longer.

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:25.390
I’ll be happy to help!

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:28.940
You mustn’t play games
for more than an hour.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.500
Honda-chan will have to design him for us.
